Pi Piper

Pi Piper (earlier working names: Open Pi and Spindle) is an independent,
community-built open-source framework for live performance. It communicates
with Native Instruments Maschine controllers over their standard USB protocol,
using only publicly documented and black-box reverse-engineered behaviour.
Pi Piper is compatible with Maschine hardware. It is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Native Instruments / inMusic Brands, Inc.
or their affiliates, and it is not made by them. Maschine, Native Instruments, and related marks are
trademarks of their respective owners and are used solely to identify
compatible third-party hardware. Pi Piper does not ship Native Instruments
logos, branding, firmware, samples, fonts, manuals, or proprietary software,
and reverse-engineering work for this project stays black-box only.
Raspberry Pi is a trademark of Raspberry Pi Ltd.
Use of Pi Piper is at your own risk.

Compatible with Native Instruments Maschine Mikro MK3 and MK3 controllers.
Shift + Stop on the controller returns to the launcher.
